::SECTION_48_RAW_INPUT_AND_HID_CAPTURE::
@FAULT_NODE [ERR-INP-001] {
    DOMAIN          : "Win32 Raw Input & Low-Level Keyboard/Mouse Hooks (RegisterRawInputDevices / WM_INPUT)"
    PHENOMENON      : "Dropped high-polling-rate mouse deltas, stuck modifier keys on Alt-Tab, or `GetRawInputData` buffer size mismatches"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Assuming a fixed `sizeof(RAWINPUT)` buffer without querying required byte size first, or failing to reset held key-state arrays upon `WM_KILLFOCUS`."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Query `GetRawInputData((HRAWINPUT)lParam, RID_INPUT, NULL, &dwSize, sizeof(RAWINPUTHEADER))` before stack/buffer allocation, mask `RI_MOUSE_MOVE_RELATIVE` vs `RI_MOUSE_MOVE_ABSOLUTE`, and clear input state vectors on `WM_KILLFOCUS`."
}

::SECTION_49_CABINET_AND_ARCHIVE_EXTRACTION::
@FAULT_NODE [ERR-ARC-001] {
    DOMAIN          : "CAB / ZIP Archive Extraction & Path Traversal Containment (SetupIterateCabinetW)"
    PHENOMENON      : "Zip-Slip / Cab-Slip arbitrary file overwrite outside `e:\\dl` target root, or partial extraction on locked destination files"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Concatenating archive member filenames directly onto the extraction directory without canonicalizing `..` segments or drive prefixes."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Canonicalize every target extraction path via `GetFullPathNameW`, verify it strictly starts with the normalized destination root prefix, and write extracted payloads atomically."
}

::SECTION_50_GDI_AND_D2D_RESOURCE_LIFECYCLES::
@FAULT_NODE [ERR-GDI-001] {
    DOMAIN          : "Win32 GDI Object Exhaustion & Direct2D Device Loss Recovery (SelectObject / D2DERR_RECREATE_TARGET)"
    PHENOMENON      : "Window rendering turning solid black/white after 10,000 GDI handle limit exhaustion, or permanent render freeze after display sleep/RDP reconnect"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Calling `DeleteObject()` on an `HBRUSH`/`HPEN`/`HFONT` while still selected into an `HDC`, or failing to release and rebuild device-dependent Direct2D resources on `D2DERR_RECREATE_TARGET`."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Always restore the original GDI object (`SelectObject(hdc, hOld)`) prior to calling `DeleteObject()`, track GDI handle counts, and handle `D2DERR_RECREATE_TARGET` by releasing and recreating render targets and brushes."
}

::MASTER_VERIFICATION_GATE::
@GATE_CHECK_F16 {
    50. RAW_INPUT_DYNAMIC  : Query `GetRawInputData` byte size dynamically and purge active key/button state maps on `WM_KILLFOCUS`.
    51. ARCHIVE_ROOT_LOCK  : Canonicalize archive entry paths and enforce strict root-prefix containment before disk extraction.
    52. GDI_D2D_RECLAIM    : Deselect GDI objects before `DeleteObject()` and rebuild Direct2D targets on `D2DERR_RECREATE_TARGET`.
}
::AVIS_MANIFEST_END::
